From: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
Date: Sat, 5 Sep 2026 15:55:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] power: supply: qcom_smbx: allow continuous 5-12 V input

Phoenix advertises and validates a 4.75-12 V TCPM input range, but the SMB5
adapter allowance is inherited from firmware.  Some powered Type-C docks leave
it in the discrete 5 V or 9-12 V mode.  A measured 8.9 V passthrough supply can
then assert USBIN_OV and pause charging even though it is inside the platform's
declared safe range.

Program the SMB5 continuous 5-12 V adapter allowance during charger probe.
This does not request a higher source voltage or bypass AICL; it only aligns the
PMIC input-valid window with the already enforced platform range.

Signed-off-by: Ankit Pipalia <ankit@example.com>
---
 drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
index 2..3 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/qcom_smbx.c
@@ -108,6 +108,10 @@
 #define AUTO_SRC_DETECT_BIT				BIT(3)
 #define HVDCP_EN_BIT					BIT(2)
 
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_CFG				0x360
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_MASK			GENMASK(3, 0)
+#define USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_5V_TO_12V			0x0c
+
 #define USBIN_LOAD_CFG					0x365
 #define ICL_OVERRIDE_AFTER_APSD_BIT			BIT(4)
 
@@ -1177,6 +1181,9 @@ static const struct smb_init_register smb5_init_seq[] = {
 	{ .addr = CHARGING_ENABLE_CMD,
 	  .mask = CHARGING_ENABLE_CMD_BIT,
 	  .val = CHARGING_ENABLE_CMD_BIT },
+	{ .addr = USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_CFG,
+	  .mask = USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_MASK,
+	  .val = USBIN_ADAPTER_ALLOW_5V_TO_12V },
 	/* Enable BC1P2 auto Src detect */
 	{ .addr = USBIN_OPTIONS_1_CFG,
 	  .mask = AUTO_SRC_DETECT_BIT,
-- 
2.51.0
